A||||13||Htown86GT||Correct Jacking points?||||5||
Z||000000||Htown86GT||04-06-2001||01:45 PM||||Hey guys I took my car to get the tires changed and the guys at the tire shop used floor jacks on both sides of my car, it looked like they got the jack close to the crossmember with the jack positioned right under the rear quarter panels, anyway when they let my car down BOTH Lower ground mouldings cracked!.....There was already a crack I made from when I jacked my car once so i told em not to worry.  Where are the best places to jack with floor jacks from the sides?  Also does anyone have some lower ground mouldings Aero style?<P>------------------<BR>86' GT  17inch Cobras Sus-tec lowered<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.rav-ee.com/images/Myfiero.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Steven||04-06-2001||01:58 PM||||Whenever I have to jack up my car to work on the rear wheels (left or right doesn't matter) I will put the floor under the engine cradle where the park brake adjuster is located, then put jack stand under the lower control arms. For the front the jack goes under the front cross member, and then put the jack stands under the lower control arms. To date, I have never jacked up the car from the side, only front or rear. <p>[This message has been edited by Steven (edited 04-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever2||04-06-2001||03:16 PM||||Man, you sure have had your share of problems.  I don't have many parts and not even much expertise, but if you ever need an extra hand or a ride or anything let me know.  I still don't know where you live, email me unless for some reason you don't want me to know.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>I have never jack[ed] up the car from the side, only front or rear.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>That goes for me too.  From all the stories I hear, it's better to take your wheels off at home and haul them to the tire store in the minivan.  That's what I did last time.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Steven||04-06-2001||03:29 PM||||Thanks for pointing out my typo. I fixed it just for you.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||04-06-2001||03:38 PM||||Please take a moment and look under the hood, the factory has conveniently placed a sticker there to indicate the correct jacking points from the sides.<BR>NO WAY! will I EVER let a shop or someone else jack OR support OR raise my Fiero(s) with a floor jack or use a lift at the sides!<BR>There is a danger with body damage (as you now know) and the greater danger in CRUSHING the coolant tubes under there. <BR>Jack stands go under the engine cradle at points of your choosing (depending on what your doing) and under the front suspension cross member, again, depending what your doing.<BR>Please take the time to review basic car care tips for your car of you (or someone else) WILL cause serious damage, at an unnecessary cost to you!||||reg||1
Z||000005||tgowens||04-06-2001||04:59 PM||||if you <I>do</I> have to jack your car up from the side do this -- look under the car on each side front and rear and you will see a flat spot on the front and rear (the spots on the rear are right in front of the front cradle mount point) of the frame........that is the ONLY point that a floor jack or pads on a lift should be placed (in the event you need to keep the cradle free).........as for me, I do the front and back with the jack stand thing, even here in the shop.........Indiana is very correct -- the bottom of that space frame is not intended to support the weight of the car and a floor jack can go right up through the floor board or worse (as he mentioned) damage the coolant tubes which run the length of both sides of the car as well as brake lines........<p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 04-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Galen||04-06-2001||07:43 PM||||I always jack my coupe up from the factory spots.. never bothered me. <P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - Sunroof, shaved emblems, more to come..<BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroLisa||04-06-2001||08:25 PM||||I've always lifted mine up from that notch on the side, and never had a problem.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Htown86GT||04-06-2001||08:53 PM||||Yup! Ive learned my lesson - Thats what I get for sitting inside in the waiting room watching TV while goofy Gus and his pals destroy whats left of my poor Fiero.....BTW its pretty hard getting a jack under the nose to find a good point on the front.. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||ThatRickGuy||04-06-2001||10:15 PM||||I throw mine up on the hoist at the hobby shop all the time. only time I had a problem was when one of the techs was lining up the other side for me. after chewing him out and showing him that the fiero is not a unibody!<P>but anyways, in the back, I use the cradle for lift points, of if I'm pulling it out, theres the rear frame points just forward of the cradle. up front there are frame points that go parellel to the coolant tubes, which are easily avoided if you spend a second to line everything up.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Galen||04-06-2001||10:24 PM||||I just read that topic again and thats something we shouldn't discuss in this forum.<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - Sunroof, shaved emblems, more to come..<BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
Z||000011||LottaBallsCamaro||04-07-2001||02:58 AM||||I like jacking in the shop...||||reg||1
Z||000012||rogergarrison||04-07-2001||09:59 AM||||I jack up mine from the notch in side all the time. Lisas too. Just have to pay attention to what your doing. And yes it will support it there just fine, that is the factory jack point and was designed for that purpose. I do put jackstands under front frame and rear cradle though.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Formula88||04-07-2001||10:53 AM||||Yea, I use the notch on the side for jacking.  Then I put jack stands under the cross member or cradle as needed.  Sure does look funny lifting the entire side of the car like that though!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
